\subsubsection{Manipulation Check}
We implement a manipulation check (see Figure~\ref{fig:procedure}) at the end of the survey to ensure that participants can distinguish between the visual styles presented. Participants are shown four consecutive, randomized images — two with a cute visual style and two with a heroic visual style. 
For each image, participants are asked to select any number of words from a list of six (cute, friendly, harmless, mighty, heroic, and powerful) that best describe the image in their opinion. These words were drawn from the prompts used for the visual styles.

