We score participants' responses as follows: one point for each correctly identified word and one point for not selecting any incorrect words. Thus, participants could earn a maximum of eight points across the four images. The majority (93.6\%) performed well, with 48.4\% scoring 8 points, 30.7\% scoring 7 points, and 14.5\% scoring 6 points. This indicates that the participants were able to differentiate between the two visual styles. 
