Computing the derivative of $\mathbb{E}[\pi_3]$ with respect to $\mathrm{\Delta}\beta$, we have
\begin{align*}  
& \frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{E}[\pi_3]}{\mathrm{d}\mathrm{\Delta\beta}} \\
=\, & \frac{\lambda_1 \lambda_2}{\lambda_1 + \lambda_2} \Bigg(  
    \frac{v_3(\alpha_{13} - 1)}{\lambda_1}   
    + \frac{v_3(\alpha_{13} - 1)}{\lambda_2}  
      \left[1 - e^{-\lambda_2 \mathrm{\Delta}\beta v_3}\right] \\
& \hspace{2.8cm}  
    - v_3^2\, \mathrm{\Delta}\beta\, e^{-\lambda_2 \mathrm{\Delta}\beta v_3}  
    - \frac{\alpha_{23} v_3\, e^{-\lambda_2 \mathrm{\Delta}\beta v_3}}{\lambda_2}  
    \Bigg) \\
<\, & 0.  
