According to Fig. \ref{p}, it is evident that the average bid ratio and average reward results of searchers exhibit less volatility compared to those of builders.
For searchers, an increase in the probability of conflicts significantly intensifies competition among them, elevating the overall level of their bid ratios while concurrently reducing their average returns, as depicted in Figs.
