Even with all the measures and strategies taken to fine-tune \textit{Granite3.2-vision:2b}, it narrowly fitted in the VRAM. The training dataset, comprising both the development and training sets, was randomly split into two parts: 90\% for training and 10\% for testing. After successfully fine-tuning on the training dataset, the model was used for inference on the final test dataset, made available later by the organisation. Apart from requiring the same dataset format adaptation into a chat format, there was no other significant step worth mentioning. This Granite approach resulted in \textbf{GRESEL2\_run1}.

