Next, we classify the set of intervals with the same color as $I_i$, as follows: 
\begin{itemize}
    \item We denote by $\mathcal{I}^{s,<}_i$ the set of intervals $I_j$ such that $x_j<x_i$ (i.e., $j<i$).
    \item We denote by $\mathcal{I}^{s,>}_i$ the set of intervals $I_j$ such that $x_j>x_i$ (i.e., $j>i$).
\end{itemize}

