At every new call of \texttt{opt}, we compute the candidate associated to an integer $k$ roughly equidistant from $i$ and $j$ (line~\ref{line:opt-3}). The answer of the decision problem for the associated candidate $q^-+\frac{1}{\alpha_k}$ indicates if the next call is \texttt{opt}$(i,k)$ or \texttt{opt}($k,j$) (lines~\ref{line:opt-11}-\ref{line:opt-8}). The algorithm terminates when $j=i+1$ (lines~\ref{line:opt-9}-\ref{line:opt-10}).

