 The values $\gamma$, $\delta$, $i$ and $j$ of Algorithm~\ref{alg:optimization} can be computed in $O(n \log^2 n)$ time by running binary search on $\left[1,{3n \choose 2}\right]$ and computing $\alpha_k$ for the values $k$ appearing in the binary search (as mentioned earlier, every such $\alpha_k$ can be computed in $O(n\log n)$ time). 
