\begin{definition}
\label{def:compatible}
A subsolution $L[k]$ is \emph{compatible} with a maximal tabular subsolution $M[i]$, for $k<i$, and, w.l.o.g., $I_i$ red, if it contains---at least---points for intervals from 1 to $i-1$ (i.e., it leaves no gaps),
and all the  blue points of $L[k]$ placed after $x_i-q$\maria{Probably only the ones corresponding to intervals with index smaller than $i$?} have intervals that start after $x_i-(1-q)$ (i.e., these points can be relocated at $x_i+q$).
\end{definition}

