    the Berth Area, the Yard Area, and the Entry-Exit Area. The Berth Area is where ships dock to load and unload containers, facilitated by quay cranes (QCs) that transfer containers between ships and trucks. The Yard Area serves as a central storage hub for temporarily housing containers before further transportation, comprising rows of container blocks with multiple stacks, where yard cranes (YCs) handle container movement between trucks and blocks. The Entry-Exit Area manages truck flow entering and exiting the terminal, connecting the terminal to external transportation networks. These areas are interconnected by road networks that guide truck movements under strict operational regulations.}
